╭─ corex 0.1.0-dev ───────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Build reliable software effortlessly at systems-level speed │
│ Usage: corex [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]…                    │
╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

Commands:
  ▸ build     Compile a CoreX package or source file into a native or WebAssembly artifact
  ▸ run       Compile and immediately execute a CoreX binary
  ▸ check     Run fast syntax, type, region, and SAST verification without codegen
  ▸ test      Compile and execute unit, snapshot, and safety verification suites
  ▸ fmt       Format CoreX source files canonically using the lossless CST
  ▸ upgrade   Apply automated AST/CST migrations and machine-applicable fixes
  ▸ lsp       Start the CoreX Language Server Protocol (LSP) daemon over stdio
  ▸ bench     Run statistical performance benchmarks and emit monochrome report tables

Global Options:
  -h, --help          Display this help menu or subcommand documentation
  -V, --version       Display the CoreX toolchain version
      --color=<when>  Configure terminal ANSI color output (default: auto)
